{"resourceIdentifier":"4721","resourceName":"CTR IPATINGA LANDFILL GAS PROJECT","description":"The proposed VCS project activity has the objective to avoid emission of Greenhouse Gases (GHG) through collection, flaring/combustion and energy use of the LFG. The proposed VCS project activity will also assist Brazil to meet its demand for energy due to the economic growing scenario, improving energy supply and contributing, at the same time, to the environmental, social and economic sustainability through climate change global mitigation and local air pollution. This initiative aims to increase renewable energy participation in relation to the total Brazilian energy consumption.\r\nPrior to the implementation of the project activity the landfill gas is being released to atmosphere and the electricity was generated by other sources in the Brazilian national electricity grid.\r\nLocated in the southeast region of Brasil, state of Minas Gerais, city of Santana do Paraíso, the proposed VCS project activity encompasses a voluntary initiative to encourage clean technology investments in the country.\r\nAs per its design configuration, combustion of collected LFG occurs in the following methane destruction device(s): \r\n-\t1 high temperature open flare;\r\n-\t2 engine-generator sets  of an electricity generation infrastructure (in which collected LFG will be utilized as gaseous fuel for electricity generation).\r\n-\tPossibility of future increase of the number of engine-generator sets, maintaining a total combined nameplate capacity up to 10 MW.","location":{"latitude":-19.443611,"longitude":-42.510556},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-12-12","endExclusive":"2024-01-12","endInclusive":"2024-01-11"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4721"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Minas Gerais"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROP